  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhanced Integrated Framework (EIF) Phase 3</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The EIF programme is a unique, multilateral support programme assisting the least developed countries to integrate into the global trade and investment system, by strengthening their productive capacities and national legal and political frameworks, and use trade as an engine for growth, sustainable development and poverty reduction. The main objective of the EIF Phase Three (2025-2031) is to foster competitive, diversified, inclusive and resilient LDC economies and to empower them to lead their sustainable  economic transformation by harnessing their trade and investment potential in a dynamic, systemic and scalable manner.

This will be achieved by:
- Strengthening the institutional and regulatory environment for trade and investment,
- Building human and institutional capacity,
- Unlocking and leveraging additional public and private financing,
- Catalysing productive capacity development in high-potential sectors,
- Deepening LDC participation in regional and global value chains.

Denmark will support EIF Phase 3 in the first three years of the programme (2025-2027).</narrative>
  </description>
